    "standardized_narrative": "Opening gross claims outstanding were $3,377.6m at 1 January 2017. Using the syndicate's gross claims development data, prior-year reserves worsened by approximately $723.2m (about 21.4% of opening reserves), a net strengthening of reserves. The movement was driven predominantly by 2013-2015 underwriting years' adverse development reflecting substantial catastrophe and large-loss exposure in 2017 (Hurricanes Harvey, Irma and Maria, Californian Wildfires, and the ADNOC refinery explosion), partly offset by releases in some earlier years and increased reinsurance recoveries.",
